WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.700
Hold onto your hats, true believers the Marvel
rumor mill has cranked out a doozy.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.100
According to We Got This Covered, anonymous
sources close to Marvel Studios have claimed

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.910
that a fourth Captain America picture is in
development one which will star Anthony Mackie,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.180
as it'll see Sam Wilson officially taking
on the mantle.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.280
Of course, we should be perfectly clear on
one point: There has been absolutely no official

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.539
word whatsoever about the possibility of a
fourth Captain America movie despite the rumors.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:32.770
This is one of those situations that begs
the question: Do we believe everything we

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.860
read online?

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.610
"The answer is: You don't."

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.200
Sam Wilson's struggle with the legacy and
shield passed on to him by Steve Rogers at

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.230
the conclusion of Avengers: Endgame is thought
to be a major focus of the upcoming Disney+

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:50.270
limited series Falcon and the Winter Soldier,
which you will note carries a reference to

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.520
Wilson's original superhero moniker right
there in its title.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.470
While we don't have all of the details yet,
we do know that the character of John Walker,

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:02.780
AKA U.S. Agent who has taken on the title
of Captain America at times in the comics

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.860
will be featured in the series, portrayed
by Wyatt Russell.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.080
Signs seem to point to some kind of struggle
over who will be the next to fill Rogers'

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.799
shoes, and this new report seems to indicate
that when the dust settles on Falcon and the

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:18.420
Winter Soldier, Wilson will have emerged as
the new, uncontested Captain America.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.880
It all makes sense on paper but is it actually
how Wilson's journey will play out?

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.860
Nobody seems to know and if they do, they're
keeping it super hush-hush.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.170
There have been a couple of conflicting comments
made by Mackie himself which suggest that

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.830
as far as Wilson taking on the mantle of Cap,
Marvel may still be weighing its options.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:40.909
First, there was the comment the star made
to MTV News back in July indicating that,

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:43.729
yes, he'd already put on the Captain America
suit.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:44.729
Mackie said:

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:46.390
"I just had my first fitting.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:50.759
It looks really good… they came to my house,
I did a fitting in my house."

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:55.240
In August, however, the actor appeared to
walk back his remarks when MTV News followed

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.630
up on the previous interview.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:57.630
He explained:

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.119
"I don't even know if the suit's in the show.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.820
And it's funny because I didn't have a fitting
for the suit.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.780
I just had my fitting and … Everybody was
like, 'Oh, you had a fitting of your suit!'

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.759
And I was like, I never said I had a fitting
for the suit.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:12.760
Go back to the tape, I said I had my first
fitting."

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.529
Yes, that is indeed what he said right after
the interviewer expressed his excitement to

00:02:17.529 --> 00:02:20.319
see him wear the Captain America suit someday
soon.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:24.540
The only thing clear here is that Mackie was
fibbing during one of those two interviews,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.989
but we'd be hard pressed to say which one.

00:02:26.989 --> 00:02:32.329
Then, consider the remark that Mackie made
at the D23 expo, also in August, when asked

00:02:32.329 --> 00:02:36.279
if Falcon and the Winter Soldier would deal
with Wilson's transition to his new role as

00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:37.569
Captain America.

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:38.569
He stated flatly:

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:40.019
"No, I am the Falcon.

00:02:40.019 --> 00:02:41.689
I will always be the Falcon.

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:43.239
The moniker will stay the same."

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:48.829
That… doesn't appear to leave a whole heck
of a lot of room for interpretation so it

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:53.109
could very well be that, despite the fact
that Rogers obviously intended for Wilson

00:02:53.109 --> 00:02:56.569
to become the new Cap, Wilson himself may
have other ideas.

00:02:56.569 --> 00:03:01.799
At any rate, Marvel's complete slate of releases
through 2022 has been announced, so if we

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:06.389
are going to get a fourth Captain America
flick, it wouldn't be until 2023 at the very

00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:07.389
earliest.

00:03:07.389 --> 00:03:10.940
Based on the information that we have available
at the moment, however, we're going to go

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.159
ahead and say that the veracity of this report
is questionable at best.

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:19.160
Of course, we'll be keeping both ears to the
ground for any additional information, and

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.900
we'll be sure to keep you informed.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.549
But Marvel has been keeping a pretty tight
lid on plot details for its Phase 4 projects,

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:29.859
so it wouldn't surprise us if we were to get
no solid leads on the studio's plans for the

00:03:29.859 --> 00:03:34.370
character of Captain America before Falcon
and the Winter Soldier premieres on Disney+

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.639
in the fall of 2020.

